// Turflang Capability Edge Case: Nested Generics & LLVM Opaque Pointers
list<list<int>> matrix
list<int> row
row.push(5)

// This seemingly perfect syntax WILL CRASH the compiler with a Type Mismatch.
// Why? Turflang translates all reference types (strings, lists, arrays) into LLVM opaque pointers.
// In Codegen.cpp, `getTurfTypeFromLLVM` sees a pointer and conservatively assumes it's a "string".
// When matrix.push(row) occurs, it checks the type of `row`. It gets "string" instead of "list<int>".
// This proves a profound architectural limitation in the current AST-LLVM translation layer!

matrix.push(row)
printline(matrix[0][0])
